# Omnical — the server submodule
#
# The whole CalDAV/CardDAV server lives in this submodule. This repo is the
# packaging/deploy/orchestration layer; the submodule is the product.
#
# ── The three repositories ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   Bytewheel/Omnical          this file's sibling: plans, runbooks, decisions
#   Bytewheel/Omnical-Code     THIS repo — CI, build, deploy, packaging
#   Bytewheel/Omnical-Server   the submodule — the server itself
#                              (fork of lennart-k/rustical v0.16.1, AGPL-3.0)
#
# All three must be public. PLAN_DEPLOYMENTS.md §10 / D2: the product is
# AGPL-3.0-or-later, so the source of the thing that actually runs has to be
# offered to the network. The running source is the submodule, not this repo.
#
# ── The URL is RELATIVE, and that is load-bearing ────────────────────────────
#
# `../Omnical-Server.git` resolves against this repo's own remote, keeping the
# OWNER and replacing only the last path segment:
#
#   https://github.com/Bytewheel/Omnical-Code.git
#     -> https://github.com/Bytewheel/Omnical-Server.git
#
# So there is no owner hardcoded anywhere, and a fork of the fork resolves to the
# fork owner's own server repo rather than back to ours. That is the point.
#
# IT MUST MATCH THE NAME OF THE SERVER REPOSITORY, exactly. A relative URL is
# not a default — git does not fall back to anything, it just builds a URL from
# it. If the two disagree, every workflow that checks out submodules dies at
# the `actions/checkout` step with `repository not found`, and a clean
# `git clone` produces an EMPTY `rustical/`. The `submodule-url-exists` job in
# `.github/workflows/hygiene.yml` exists to turn that into one sentence; it was
# added after exactly this happened on 2026-09-28.
#
# Per PLAN_DEPLOYMENTS.md §5.2.4 the previous state of this repo was a gitlink
# with NO .gitmodules, so `git clone` produced an empty `rustical/` and the
# build could not start at all. This file is what fixes that — but only if the
# repository it names actually exists.

[submodule "rustical"]
	path = rustical
	url = ../Omnical-Server.git
	branch = omnical-scheduling
